    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0630" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg610"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 16, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: Another week has passed, and the
                    British subjects taken on board British vessels seized for breach of blockade
                    are still in prison. I must beg you to look back to my letter of the 9th, and I
                    must express a hope that you will at least enable me to inform her Majesty’s
                    government, by the mail of to-morrow, that the <hi rendition="#italic">five</hi>
                    men lately belonging to the Don, who have been so long confined in the Ludlow
                    street jail, have at last been set free.</p>
                <p>Believe me to be, my dear sir, your very faithful, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
